  Object cases Number, Text have no valid discriminant.
  
  Runtime field "kind" overlaps between cases Number and Text at literal
  "special". Literal-first overlap involving GADT constructors is not
  supported because matching a different constructor can change its type
  refinements. Use disjoint discriminator values or types.
  
  Give every object case a required immutable field with the same JavaScript
  property name and distinguishable runtime values or types. A literal may
  precede a broader type only when the remaining payload fields have matching
  runtime names, types, optionality and mutability.